      zh: `孔子曰：「貞以幹之，敬以輔之；施仁無倦；見君子則舉之，見小人則退之。去汝惡心，而忠與之。效其行，修其禮；千里之外，親如兄弟。行不效，禮不修；則對門不汝通矣。夫終日言，不遺己之憂；終日行，不遺己之患；唯智者能之。故自修者，必恐懼以除患，恭儉以避難者也。終身為善，一言則敗之。可不慎乎？」`,
      en: `Confucius said, "Be upright to stem it, reverent to assist it; bestow benevolence without weariness; seeing a gentleman promote him, seeing a petty man withdraw from him. Remove your evil heart and be loyal with him. Emulate his conduct, cultivate his ritual — a thousand li away, as close as brothers. If conduct is not emulated, ritual not cultivated — then even opposite your door he will not admit you. To speak all day without leaving self's worries, to act all day without leaving self's troubles — only the wise can do this. Therefore one who self-cultivates must use fear and reverence to remove trouble, respect and frugality to avoid calamity. To be good all one's life — one word can ruin it. Can one not be careful?"`
